.Dd August 17, 2026
.Dt GENTLSA 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm gentlsa
.Nd configuration files for GenTLSA publishers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /etc/gentlsa/cloudflare.cfg
.Pa /etc/gentlsa/nsupdate.cfg
.Pa /etc/gentlsa/route53.cfg
.Pa /etc/gentlsa/google.cfg
.Pa /etc/gentlsa/azure.cfg
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr gentlsa 1
reads INI-style files for each DNS publisher.
The first existing path wins.
Environment variables override values from the file.
.Pp
System paths under
.Pa /etc/gentlsa
are preferred.
Per-user fallbacks are listed with each file.
.Ss Cloudflare
.Pa /etc/gentlsa/cloudflare.cfg ,
then
.Pa ~/.cloudflare/cloudflare.cfg .
Section name
.Sy CloudFlare
or
.Sy Cloudflare .
.Pp
A scoped API token
.Pq no email
is preferred:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[CloudFlare]
token = <api token>
.Ed
.Pp
.Sy api_token
and
.Sy apitoken
are accepted as aliases for
.Sy token .
A global API key still works if both email and token are set:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[CloudFlare]
email = <cloudflare login>
token = <global API key>
.Ed
.Pp
The token needs Zone read and DNS edit on the zones you publish to.
.Bl -tag -width CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
.It Ev CF_API_TOKEN , Ev CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
Bearer API token.
.It Ev CF_API_EMAIL , Ev CLOUDFLARE_EMAIL
Login for a global API key.
.It Ev CF_API_KEY , Ev CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY
Global API key.
.El
.Ss nsupdate
RFC 2136 dynamic updates signed with TSIG.
.Nm
does not shell out to the BIND
.Xr nsupdate 1
binary.
.Pp
.Pa /etc/gentlsa/nsupdate.cfg ,
then
.Pa ~/.gentlsa/nsupdate.cfg .
Section name
.Sy Nsupdate ,
.Sy nsupdate ,
or
.Sy NSUpdate .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[Nsupdate]
server = ns1.example.com
port = 53
key-name = gentlsa-update.
secret = <base64 hmac>
algorithm = hmac-sha256
ttl = 3600
.Ed
.Pp
.Sy hmac-sha256
is the default and the recommended algorithm.
.Sy hmac-sha384
and
.Sy hmac-sha512
are also accepted.
The secret is BIND-style base64; hex is accepted too.
Default port is 53; default TTL is 3600.
.Pp
Key aliases:
.Sy host , nameserver , ns
for
.Sy server ;
.Sy key_name , keyname , name
for
.Sy key-name ;
.Sy key , key-secret
for
.Sy secret ;
.Sy alg , hmac
for
.Sy algorithm .
.Pp
.Cm list Fl -nsupdate
without ports tries AXFR.
If the key is not allowed to transfer the zone, pass the ports
instead.
The nameserver must allow UPDATE
.Pq and AXFR, if you want port-less list
for that TSIG key on the zone.
.Bl -tag -width GENTLSA_NSUPDATE_ALGORITHM
.It Ev GENTLSA_NSUPDATE_SERVER
Nameserver host.
.It Ev GENTLSA_NSUPDATE_PORT
Nameserver port
.Pq default 53 .
.It Ev GENTLSA_NSUPDATE_KEY_NAME
TSIG key name.
.It Ev GENTLSA_NSUPDATE_SECRET
TSIG secret.
.It Ev GENTLSA_NSUPDATE_ALGORITHM
.Sy hmac-sha256 ,
.Sy hmac-sha384 ,
or
.Sy hmac-sha512 .
.It Ev GENTLSA_NSUPDATE_TTL
TTL for new records
.Pq default 3600 .
.El
.Ss Route 53
Amazon Route 53 REST API
.Pq SigV4 .
.Pa /etc/gentlsa/route53.cfg ,
then
.Pa ~/.gentlsa/route53.cfg .
Section name
.Sy Route53 ,
.Sy route53 ,
or
.Sy AWS .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[Route53]
access_key = AKIA...
secret_key = ...
ttl = 3600
.Ed
.Pp
.Sy session_token
is accepted for temporary credentials.
Default TTL is 3600.
The IAM principal needs
.Sy route53:ListHostedZones ,
.Sy route53:ListResourceRecordSets ,
and
.Sy route53:ChangeResourceRecordSets
on the hosted zones you publish to.
.Bl -tag -width GENTLSA_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
.It Ev AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID , Ev GENTLSA_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID
Access key.
.It Ev AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY , Ev GENTLSA_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
Secret key.
.It Ev AWS_SESSION_TOKEN , Ev GENTLSA_AWS_SESSION_TOKEN
Session token
.Pq optional .
.El
.Ss Google Cloud DNS
.Pa /etc/gentlsa/google.cfg ,
then
.Pa ~/.gentlsa/google.cfg .
Section name
.Sy Google ,
.Sy google ,
or
.Sy GCP .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[Google]
credentials = /etc/gentlsa/google-sa.json
project = my-gcp-project
ttl = 3600
.Ed
.Pp
.Sy credentials_file
and
.Sy key_file
are aliases for
.Sy credentials .
The project can also come from
.Sy project_id
in the service-account JSON.
Default TTL is 3600.
.Pp
The service account needs
.Sy dns.managedZones.list ,
.Sy dns.resourceRecordSets.list ,
and
.Sy dns.changes.create
.Pq DNS Administrator, or a custom role with those permissions .
.Bl -tag -width GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS
.It Ev GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS , Ev GENTLSA_GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS
Path to service-account JSON.
.It Ev GENTLSA_GOOGLE_PROJECT , Ev GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT , Ev GCLOUD_PROJECT
GCP project.
.El
.Ss Azure DNS
Azure Resource Manager DNS API
.Pq TLSA via 2023-07-01-preview .
.Pa /etc/gentlsa/azure.cfg ,
then
.Pa ~/.gentlsa/azure.cfg .
Section name
.Sy Azure ,
.Sy azure ,
or
.Sy AzureDNS .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[Azure]
tenant_id = <directory id>
client_id = <application id>
client_secret = <client secret>
subscription_id = <subscription id>
resource_group = <resource group>
ttl = 3600
.Ed
.Pp
.Sy tenant , client-id , app_id , secret ,
and
.Sy subscription
are accepted as aliases.
.Sy credentials , credentials_file ,
and
.Sy key_file
can point at an Azure service-principal JSON file.
.Sy resource_group
is optional; when omitted,
.Nm
lists every DNS zone in the subscription.
Default TTL is 3600.
Azure only accepts TLSA records on a DNSSEC-signed zone.
.Pp
The principal needs
.Sy Microsoft.Network/dnszones/read
plus
.Sy Microsoft.Network/dnszones/TLSA/read ,
.Sy write ,
and
.Sy delete
.Pq DNS Zone Contributor, or a custom role with those permissions .
.Bl -tag -width GENTLSA_AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID
.It Ev AZURE_TENANT_ID , Ev GENTLSA_AZURE_TENANT_ID
Directory
.Pq tenant
ID.
.It Ev AZURE_CLIENT_ID , Ev GENTLSA_AZURE_CLIENT_ID
Application
.Pq client
ID.
.It Ev AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET , Ev GENTLSA_AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET
Client secret.
.It Ev AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID , Ev GENTLSA_AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID
Subscription ID.
.It Ev AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP , Ev GENTLSA_AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP
Resource group
.Pq optional .
.It Ev GENTLSA_AZURE_CREDENTIALS , Ev AZURE_CREDENTIALS
Path to service-principal JSON.
.El
.Ss Unsupported
DigitalOcean DNS is not supported: the official API has no TLSA
record type and no DNSSEC.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/gentlsa.conf
.It Pa /etc/gentlsa/cloudflare.cfg
Cloudflare credentials.
.It Pa ~/.cloudflare/cloudflare.cfg
Per-user Cloudflare fallback.
.It Pa /etc/gentlsa/nsupdate.cfg
RFC 2136 / TSIG settings.
.It Pa ~/.gentlsa/nsupdate.cfg
Per-user nsupdate fallback.
.It Pa /etc/gentlsa/route53.cfg
Route 53 credentials.
.It Pa ~/.gentlsa/route53.cfg
Per-user Route 53 fallback.
.It Pa /etc/gentlsa/google.cfg
Google Cloud DNS settings.
.It Pa ~/.gentlsa/google.cfg
Per-user Google fallback.
.It Pa /etc/gentlsa/azure.cfg
Azure DNS settings.
.It Pa ~/.gentlsa/azure.cfg
Per-user Azure fallback.
.It Pa /var/lib/gentlsa/rollover
System directory for persisted
.Cm rollover
jobs.
Created on Linux by
.Pa /usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/gentlsa.conf .
Override with
.Ev GENTLSA_STATE_DIR .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gentlsa 1 ,
.Xr nsupdate 1
